From 717f43dec3ba5e209f5db47162c039dd6ee6c36b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shane Williams <44717004+KingHavok@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 14:08:30 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Support external authentication providers in front of Home
 Assistant

Keep main-frame authentication-provider navigation inside the WebView so that
OIDC / OAuth 2.0 reverse proxies (Cloudflare Access, Authelia, Authentik, Vouch,
oauth2-proxy) can complete their interactive sign-in inside the app instead of
being ejected to the system browser, where the resulting session cookie never
returns to the app's WebView.

TLSWebViewClient gains a `serverHost` anchor and an override of
shouldOverrideUrlLoading(WebResourceRequest) that keeps two kinds of navigation
in-WebView: server-initiated http(s) redirects on the main frame (the proxy
challenge and its return redirect), and any main-frame http(s) navigation while
the WebView is currently on a host other than the anchored Home Assistant origin
(so federated-IdP buttons on a proxy login page are not ejected mid-flow).
Everything else falls through to the existing URL-interception path, so
user-tapped external links from the HA frontend still open in the system browser.

The anchor is set by FrontendViewModel (when it selects the server URL to load)
and by the onboarding ConnectionViewModel. This replaces an earlier version that
attached the same behaviour to WebViewActivity, which upstream has since removed
in favour of FrontendScreen / FrontendViewModel.

Known limitation: Google / Microsoft federated sign-in refuses to render in any
embedded WebView (Error 403: disallowed_useragent) by published provider policy;
use a non-federated factor (email OTP, TOTP, WebAuthn) or a self-hosted IdP.

Based on closed upstream PR home-assistant/android#6725.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
